cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the Queyi datasets, real-world benchmark, or tooling, please cite this repository."
title: "Caliber Drift and Capability Boundaries: An Audit Protocol for Software-Verification Evaluation"
abstract: >-
  Queyi is a research line and reproducible audit toolchain for software-verification
  evaluation: it asks whether an apparently convincing evaluation result survives an
  audit of the evaluator that produced it. It ships a measurement-drift algebra (caliber
  signature, four drift types, seven axioms), a capability-boundary map of the instrument,
  and a real-world validation arm. This repository also hosts (a) a 1,147-sample x 8-asset
  frozen detection matrix with four-state verdicts (pass/fail/unknown/contradict) and an
  append-only ledger with Merkle integrity, and (b) a real-world benchmark of reconstructed
  C++ defects with traceable CVE/issue/commit provenance and NVD-verified metadata.
